# minted DOI record and cannot be edited afterwards for a tagged release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this platform or its reference libraries, please cite the software record (and the manuscript once published)."
title: "PlantVirusAnalysisPlatform: an offline-deployable web platform for end-to-end plant virus detection, quantification and evolutionary analysis on Windows workstations"
abstract: >-
  PlantVirusAnalysisPlatform is a Windows-native, fully offline platform that runs a
  15-stage plant virus analysis pipeline (host depletion, dual-engine known-virus
  identification and quantification, de novo assembly, consensus calling, ORF
  annotation, phylogenetics, recombination and primer design) behind a local web
  UI, a CLI and an MCP server.
type: software
version: 1.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/zhangwenda0518/PlantVirusAnalysisPlatform"
url: "https://github.com/zhangwenda0518/PlantVirusAnalysisPlatform"
keywords:
  - plant virology
  - virus detection
  - high-throughput sequencing
  - bioinformatics pipeline
  - reproducible analysis
  - offline software
authors:
